{
  "children": [
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Determination of the speed of sound in air by resonance-tube method",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "type": "Title"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "A. Student — PHYS 2010 Lab, Group 4B",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "type": "Author"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Objective",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "To determine the speed of sound in air at room temperature by measuring the resonance lengths of a closed tube driven by tuning forks of known frequency, and to compare the result with the accepted value.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Theory",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "A closed cylindrical tube supports standing waves when the air column length satisfies the resonance condition for odd multiples of a quarter wavelength. For the ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "n",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": "-th resonance (",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "n = 1, 3, 5, \\ldots",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ") the effective length is",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "latex": "L_n + \\epsilon = \\frac{n \\lambda}{4},\\qquad n = 1, 3, 5, \\ldots",
      "numbered": true,
      "label": "eq:resonance",
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "where ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "L_n",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " is the measured length from the open end to the water surface, ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\epsilon",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " is the end correction (approximately ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "0.6 r",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " for a tube of radius ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "r",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": "), and ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\lambda = v / f",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " is the wavelength corresponding to frequency ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "f",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " and speed ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "v",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Eliminating the end correction between two successive resonances gives",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "latex": "v = 2 f (L_3 - L_1).",
      "numbered": true,
      "label": "eq:speed",
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Apparatus",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Glass resonance tube (length 100 cm, inner diameter 3.4 cm) with adjustable water reservoir",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Tuning forks: 256 Hz, 440 Hz, 512 Hz (calibrated ±0.5 Hz)",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Metre ruler (±0.5 mm) and vernier caliper (±0.02 mm)",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Digital thermometer (±0.1 °C)",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Rubber mallet for striking the tuning forks",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        }
      ],
      "type": "List"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Procedure",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "ordered": true,
      "items": [
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Record ambient temperature and atmospheric pressure.",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Strike the 256 Hz tuning fork and hold it at the open end of the tube.",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Slowly lower the water level until the first loud resonance is heard; record L₁.",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Continue lowering until the second resonance is heard; record L₃.",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Repeat three times and average.",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Repeat for the 440 Hz and 512 Hz forks.",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        }
      ],
      "type": "List"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Data",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Room temperature: ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "T = 21.3 \\pm 0.1",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " °C. Atmospheric pressure: 1013 hPa.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "rows": [
        [
          "Fork (Hz)",
          "Trial",
          "L₁ (cm)",
          "L₃ (cm)"
        ],
        [
          "256",
          "1",
          "31.8",
          "98.2"
        ],
        [
          "256",
          "2",
          "31.6",
          "98.0"
        ],
        [
          "256",
          "3",
          "31.9",
          "98.4"
        ],
        [
          "440",
          "1",
          "18.2",
          "57.3"
        ],
        [
          "440",
          "2",
          "18.4",
          "57.1"
        ],
        [
          "440",
          "3",
          "18.3",
          "57.4"
        ],
        [
          "512",
          "1",
          "15.6",
          "49.0"
        ],
        [
          "512",
          "2",
          "15.5",
          "48.8"
        ],
        [
          "512",
          "3",
          "15.7",
          "49.1"
        ]
      ],
      "caption": "Measured resonance lengths for three tuning forks.",
      "label": "tab:data",
      "alignment": "llrr",
      "style": "",
      "type": "Table"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Analysis",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Applying Equation ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "label": "eq:speed",
          "kind": "eqref",
          "type": "CrossRef"
        },
        {
          "text": " to the averaged lengths for the 256 Hz fork:",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "latex": "v = 2 \\times 256 \\times (0.982 - 0.318) = 340.2\\;\\text{m/s}.",
      "numbered": false,
      "label": null,
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Repeating for all three forks:",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "rows": [
        [
          "Fork (Hz)",
          "v (m/s)"
        ],
        [
          "256",
          "340.2 ± 1.8"
        ],
        [
          "440",
          "343.1 ± 2.1"
        ],
        [
          "512",
          "342.0 ± 1.6"
        ]
      ],
      "caption": "Speed of sound derived from each tuning fork.",
      "label": "tab:results",
      "alignment": "lr",
      "style": "",
      "type": "Table"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The weighted mean is ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "v = 341.6 \\pm 1.0",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " m/s. The accepted value at 21.3 °C is",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "latex": "v_{\\text{ref}} = 331.3 + 0.606 \\times 21.3 = 344.2\\;\\text{m/s},",
      "numbered": false,
      "label": null,
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "giving a percentage discrepancy of 0.8%, which is within the combined uncertainty.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Discussion",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The systematic under-estimate may be partly explained by the end correction: the simple formula ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\epsilon \\approx 0.6 r",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " assumes an infinite baffle, whereas our open tube end radiates into free space. Additionally, the tuning forks may have drifted slightly from their nominal frequencies with age. A future experiment could use a frequency counter to verify the fork output directly.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Conclusion",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The speed of sound in air was measured as ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "341.6 \\pm 1.0",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " m/s at 21.3 °C, consistent with the expected value of 344.2 m/s within experimental uncertainty. The resonance-tube method provides a straightforward and reliable measurement of the speed of sound.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    }
  ],
